3. Source datasets of the benchmark: not relicensed, and not in git
-------------------------------------------------------------------

The benchmark's samples and the raw model answers are not part of this
repository (bench/*/data/ and bench/*/results/ are not tracked). The
published per-sample verdict tables hold sample ids, labels and verdicts,
not the samples' text. Each source keeps its own licence. As recorded in
this repository:

  SusVibes (LeiLiLab)                          MIT
      security vulnerability
  Collu-Bench (lt-asset)                       BSD-3-Clause-Clear
      logic error
  SWE-rebench-OpenHands-Trajectories (Nebius)  CC-BY-4.0
      incomplete execution; the base patches of scope creep, supply chain
      and dependency blindness
  Delulu (microsoft/delulu)                    per-row licences, some of
      fabrication                              them non-commercial (noted
                                               in the review of 2026-11-21;
                                               not recorded per row here)
  Patronus TRACE (PatronusAI/trace-dataset)    CC-BY-SA-4.0, access on
      test manipulation                        request (same note)
  Wang et al., deprecated-API map (ICSE'25)    no licence on the source
      obsolescence                             repository; only API names
                                               are used
  OpenSSF malicious-packages                   package names only; licence
      supply chain                             not recorded here

Before any per-sample release, each source's redistribution terms must be
checked one by one; where a licence does not allow redistribution, publish
sample ids and a build script instead of the text.

One tracked file does republish third-party samples:
bench/labelcheck/site/items.json (70 items for a blind label check). Each
item names its source dataset and licence (SWE-rebench and
SWE-rebench-OpenHands-Trajectories, Nebius, CC-BY-4.0; SusVibes, LeiLiLab,
MIT). The projects the patches come from keep their own licences.


